    "body": "- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n\nWhilst reading both docs and code, I found some typos.\nThere is a [part](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/4084a97fb06593e7f3855a9c5c63f1b87ae225e3/lua/mini/test.lua#L1423) I found confusing:\n\n```txt\n---     - `child.api.nvim_buf_line_count(0)` will execute\n---       `vim.api.nvim_buf_line_count(0)` inside child process and return its\n```\n\nIt does not execute `vim.api.nvim_buf_line_count(0)` literally. Perhaps:\n\n```txt\n---     - `child.api.nvim_buf_line_count(0)` will execute\n---       `nvim_buf_line_count(0)`(see `:h api`) inside child process and return its\n```\n ",
