            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> There is a [part](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/4084a97fb06593e7f3855a9c5c63f1b87ae225e3/lua/mini/test.lua#L1423) I found confusing:\r\n> \r\n> ```\r\n> ---     - `child.api.nvim_buf_line_count(0)` will execute\r\n> ---       `vim.api.nvim_buf_line_count(0)` inside child process and return its\r\n> ```\r\n\r\nIndeed it is not *quite* `child.lua('vim.api.nvim_buf_line_count(0)')`, but the Lua form is more understandable than using the API. If it will make it clearer, maybe replace \"will execute\" with \"will act as if\"?",
